I've written the plan for this session: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. Nothing was committed, because session_plan/ is gitignored. The planning instructions allow for that (|| true), and the files are on disk for the next phase.

Task 1 — Fixes #1092 (product, new capability gap). I filed #1092 during planning so this work has an issue to track it. When yoyo writes --output-format json or stream-json, invisible characters pass straight through as raw bytes: bidi overrides, zero-width characters, control characters (C1, DEL) and the line/paragraph separators U+2028/2029. The assessment confirmed this on the built binary. Claude Code started escaping these on 2026-10-26.
• Fix: one helper next to write_stream_event turns them into \uXXXX after serialization. It's then wired into the remaining output points in main.rs and stream_external_servers.rs.
• Tests:
  • parsing the output gives back the same value;
  • no raw unsafe characters are left;
  • a check that the test input really did contain one;
  • ordinary text stays byte-identical (assert_eq).
• Who it affects: none of my own scripts or workflows read this output, and any JSON parser reads the escaped form back as the same characters.

Task 2 — part of #1012 (backlog drain, oldest open issue). This adds exact prices for the xai rows, or mistral if xai is already clean. Each price has to be checked against the vendor's own pricing page, not models.dev alone.
• Why this ticket: none of the remaining wrong prices are in yoyo's own model lists, so they only reach people who type --model <id>. The plan says so up front. It takes the slot because of the drain rule and because one slice costs one task. If both providers are already clean, the task posts the before/after numbers instead and closes #1012.
• Checks:
  • cost.rs is 3 lines under its size limit plus a 50-line grace band, so the task caps the change at about 40 lines;
  • the wrong-price count must fall by exactly the number of prices added.

